flowchart TB
  accTitle: Federation preserves local autonomy
  accDescr: Community A keeps its governance, membership and private case data locally, and Community B does the same. Selected information moves from A to B only through an agreed exchange policy and synchronization filters that respect the originator's permissions. Permitted sightings and corrections can return from B to A. Connectivity does not authorise onward sharing.

  subgraph a["Community A"]
    alocal["Own governance and membership<br/>Private case data stays local"]:::muted
    ashare["Local sharing platform"]:::accent
    alocal -->|Approve selected findings| ashare
  end

  gate["Agreed exchange policy<br/>and synchronization filters"]

  subgraph b["Community B"]
    bshare["Local sharing platform"]:::accent
    blocal["Own governance and membership<br/>Private case data stays local"]:::muted
    bshare -->|Apply local handling rules| blocal
  end

  ashare -->|Select information permitted to leave| gate
  gate -->|Preserve provenance and markings| bshare
  bshare -.->|Permitted sightings and corrections| ashare
